  "regressions": [
    "Real HTTP grouped query preserves scoped auth, search/platform/recent and page offset, with returned sibling fields.",
    "Controller selects the second tagged version from one Store card; only that ROM ID reaches transfer/publication.",
    "Cancel, permission failure, wrong returned identity and held selection after profile switch do not write a game.",
    "Modal first selection retains focus across resize even when the background detail layout is rebuilt.",
    "Logo endpoint/mime/dimension filtering, round-trip and partial-artwork replacement preserve other images and ROM bytes.",
    "Home paints the decoded selected logo instead of text; disabled artwork restores text and poster/background fallbacks.",
    "Notification expiry/newer timers, page geometry, unchanged focus, ongoing progress, account reset and game-active return."
  ],
  "investigations": [
    "Initial fixture compile used the wrong DownloadProgress import; corrected without changing production behavior.",
    "Initial version Cancel autofocus captured loading focus; it now autofocuses only an idle error/no-selection state.",
    "Renderer showed resize moving focus to the underlying Download button; route-aware autofocus and a deterministic resize assertion fixed it.",
    "Final feedback observation found a silent game-active field transition; emitting the changed state ensures return errors appear.",
    "The renderer imports Flutter-exported typed data; an unnecessary import analyzer finding was corrected.",
    "Initial package verification reported a modified nested App.framework while both nested frameworks validated independently. The generated development bundle was explicitly re-sealed with the existing Release entitlements and the final built/extracted archive verified; no framework or application code was changed by signing. The precise Xcode incremental-build cause is not established. See signature-repair.json."
